<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Steps 3-4: the descent result</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L6" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># Steps 3-4 of Example 7: gamma = gamma_1/3 + gamma_0/2 with
#   gamma_1(chi) = 3(y chi_y + x chi_x) theta,  gamma_0(chi) = -2 chi (x theta_x + y theta_y),
# i.e. gamma(chi) = (y chi_y + x chi_x) theta - chi (x theta_x + y theta_y).
# Theorem 1, eq. (6.3), asserts OP = d_0 o gamma only on E_X, so the residual Z below
# is NOT identically zero: it vanishes modulo the relations of E_X, i.e. theta_xx + theta_yy = 0,
# y theta_x - x theta_y = 0, and their total derivatives.
sgn2 := 1:
gam := evalDG( (y*TotalDiff(v1[],[2]) + x*TotalDiff(v1[],[1])) * Cu1[]
   - v1[] * (x*Cu1[1] + y*Cu1[2]) ):
Z := evalDG( OP - sgn2*HorizontalExteriorDerivative(gam) );
# CHECK 3 (expect 0): restriction of Z to E_X. Rotationally invariant harmonic functions
# are u = A log(x^2 + y^2) + B (A, B constants), so on E_X every Cartan form theta_alpha
# equals D_alpha(A log(x^2 + y^2) + B) dA-wise; since Z is linear in the theta's, its restriction
# to E_X vanishes iff the contraction with the (prolonged) evolutionary field of
# characteristic A log(x^2 + y^2) + B is zero for arbitrary constants A, B.
E_inv := Prolong( evalDG( (A*log(x^2 + y^2) + B) * D_u1[] ), K ):
simplify( evalDG( Hook(E_inv, Z) ) );</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L7" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># omega_gamma = (y theta_y + x theta_x) ^ theta is obtained from gamma by writing D_alpha(chi)
# on the left and replacing it by (1/p) theta_alpha ^ (p = 2); omega_gamma|_{E_X} represents the reduction.
omega_gamma := evalDG( (y*Cu1[2] + x*Cu1[1]) &amp;wedge Cu1[] );</Text-field>
</Input>
